\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For axisymmetric initial data with ADM mass $m$ and total angular momentum $J_\infty$, prove $m\geq\sqrt{|J_\infty|}$ for manifolds with a trapped inner boundary. For multiple black holes satisfying $m\geq\mathcal M_{\mathrm{many}}$, determine the value and parameter dependence of $\mathcal M_{\mathrm{many}}$ and identify the geometric meaning of its minimizer.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2018/36}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For axisymmetric initial data with ADM mass $m$ and total angular momentum $J_\infty$, prove $m\geq\sqrt{|J_\infty|}$ for manifolds with a trapped inner boundary. For multiple black holes satisfying $m\geq\mathcal M_{\mathrm{many}}$, determine the value and parameter dependence of $\mathcal M_{\mathrm{many}}$ and identify the geometric meaning of its minimizer.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30003917 (OWR-16411-010). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2018/36}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:30003917}

